      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: Replacing Missing with reference to prefab asset is done by Unity.\n\nActually, unity doesn't do replace missing with reference to component assets in prefab, Unity forget to replace Missing with None instead.\n\nIf we modified the PhysBone component just after PhysBoneCollider removal, Missing reference to PhysBoneCollider in PhysBone component will be replaced with None with a prefab overrides.\n\nIn the prefab, all reference to Components/GameObjects in the prefab itself is done with reference to assets in prefab itself, and replaced with instantiated GameObject/Component on instantiation of the prefab. \n\nAlso, Unity keeps reference to assets in the prefab if the instantiated GameObject/Component does not exists.\n\nIf we removed some GameObject/Component using prefab overrides, until next instantiation, the reference will be Missing (UnityEngine.Object which is marked as destoryed).\n\nHowever, on the next instantiation of prefab, instantiated GameObject/Component will not be exists so it looks missing is replaced with reference to prefab.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-06-16T13:29:45.778Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When using prefab workflow, there may be unwanted references to PhysBoneColliders of prefab assets.\n\n1. Place an avatar prefab into the scene.\n\n2. Remove a PhysBoneCollider referenced by PhysBones.\n\n3. Start Play Mode then stop.\n\nAfter step 3, PhysBones' colliders parameter refers PhysBoneCollider of **prefab asset** instead of \"Missing\".\n\nIn this situation, unwanted assets such as materials referenced by prefab only are included in the built avatar.\n\nTo avoid this behavior, I suggest to remove such unwanted reference in SDK's build process.",
